    "raw": "Repo: jovlinger/utils, skills/projectmanagement/todos (todo.py, todo_web.py, SKILL.md).\nParent: 5b446160 (grooming backlog). This implements its item 1 (state renames) and\nthe state-filter half of item 3, plus the new requirements below.\n\nGOAL\n`todo ls` and `todo search` hide terminated states (done, merged) by default.\nImplemented via -s handling + a new --states filter with a macro grammar.\n\nA. DEFAULT HIDING + -s / --states MODEL (confirmed)\nFilter precedence:  --states  >  -s (= ALL)  >  config default (ALL,-FINAL).\n  - neither flag   -> config.json default filter (default ALL,-FINAL) -> hide done/merged; no State column.\n  - -s             -> filter = ALL (unhide everything) AND render the State column.\n  - --states=X     -> filter = X (State column shown, since states were named).\n  - -s --states=X  -> filter = X AND render the State column.\n-s keeps its current meaning of \"show the State column\" (today's _add_column_args)\nin addition to lifting the default hide. Applies to BOTH ls and search.\nNOTE: ls has no state filtering today; search has an optional --state (singular)\nfilter with no default -- both migrate to this model. Rename singular --state -> --states.\n\nB. --states GRAMMAR\nMandatory value (comma list). Reuses the existing +/-/, left-to-right evaluation\n(parse_state_filter): ',' and '+' = union, '-' = difference, evaluated left to right\nAFTER inline macro expansion. Example: ALL,-done shows everything except done.\nDefault (no -s, no --states, no config override) = ALL,-FINAL.\nCasing convention: concrete state names lowercase; MACROS uppercase, so a token is\nunambiguously a state or a macro.\nMacros:\n  ALL       = every state\n  FINAL     = done, merged        (hidden by default)\n  PAUSING   = waiting, userneeded, stopped\n  WORKING   = working             [OPEN: include ready? old 'run' alias = ready+working]\n  UNSTARTED = groom, ready        [OPEN: ready boundary vs WORKING]\n  INFO      = fact\nN/a is a member of ALL only.\nReplace the old lowercase aliases (all/todo/stall/run) with these macros\n(default: drop them; optionally keep as deprecated synonyms).\n\nC. config.json DEFAULT FILTER\nStore the default filter expression under a new key in <basedir>/.todo/config.json\n(same file as the storage DSN / version marker). Absent key -> built-in ALL,-FINAL.\n\nD. STATE RENAMES + FACT (confirmed)\n  pre       -> groom\n  pre-init  -> groom     (both collapse into GROOM)\n  init      -> ready\n  info      -> fact      (migrate the info STATE to fact)\nAdd fact as a valid state: an informational todo that will never be worked; it exists\nto harness vector-memory associative recall. fact is the sole State of such an \"info\nobject\". Principle (from parent todo): prefer nouns over gerunds.\nUpdate VALID_STATES, mint/init/set defaults + help text, argparse choices lists, and\nany TERMINAL/state-group references. Stored State keys stay lowercase (groom/ready/fact);\nUPPERCASE is reserved for macros -- confirm final casing at implementation.\nMIGRATION: renaming stored State keys needs a data migration for existing todos\n(pre/pre-init->groom, init->ready, info->fact) via the migrate-to-latest framework\n(schema_version / RECORD_MIGRATIONS), not an ad hoc pass. Both backends (sqlite + file).\n\nE. SUBTODO_STATE_INFO IS A DIFFERENT NAMESPACE (do NOT conflate)\nSUBTODO_STATE_INFO = \"INFO\" (todo.py ~1481) is a Subtodos back-link marker inserted by\n`set --parent` (a follow-only HATEOAS link, excluded from merge-completeness) -- NOT a\ntodo's own State. The info->fact STATE migration MUST NOT touch these Subtodos INFO\nmarkers. Verify no code path conflates the two before migrating.\n\nF. SKILL UPDATES (SKILL.md + any skill references)\n  - Document the new state vocabulary (groom, ready, fact + the rest) and the\n    noun-over-gerund principle.\n  - Document the selection commands: ls/search hide FINAL by default; -s shows all +\n    State column; --states=<expr> with the macro grammar. Worked examples, e.g.:\n      todo ls                                  # active work (FINAL hidden)\n      todo ls -s                               # everything, with State column\n      todo search foo --states=WORKING,PAUSING\n      todo search foo --states=ALL,-done\n      todo ls --states=FACT                    # browse the fact / memory corpus\n  - FACT extra verification: when the skill/agent is asked to WORK a fact todo, it MUST\n    pause and ask for explicit confirmation first (facts are memory anchors, not work\n    items).\n\nOPEN / TO CONFIRM AT GROOMING\n  - WORKING/UNSTARTED boundary: does WORKING include ready? (default WORKING={working},\n    UNSTARTED={groom,ready}).\n  - Keep old lowercase aliases as deprecated synonyms, or drop (default: drop).\n  - Final stored-state casing (lowercase assumed).\n  - Should ls keep its current column-driven sort when a state filter is active?\n\nACCEPTANCE (tests)\n  - ls/search hide done+merged by default; -s reveals them + adds the State column.\n  - --states macro expansion + include/-exclude, left-to-right (ALL,-done etc.).\n  - config.json default override honored; absent -> ALL,-FINAL.\n  - Migration renames pre/pre-init->groom, init->ready, info->fact on both stores;\n    SUBTODO_STATE_INFO markers untouched.\n  - SKILL.md documents states + selection examples + FACT-work verification."
  },
